$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4.2. Ethyl
4-(2-Bromophenyl)-6-methoxy-1,5-naphthyridine-3-carboxylate (4a) (Typical
Procedure; See Table 1, Entry 1). Ethyl
4-bromo-6-methoxy-1,5-naphthyridine-3-carboxylate (2b) (310 mg, 1 mmol),
K2CO3 (279 mg, 2 equiv), Pd(dppf)Cl2 3DCM (41 mg, 0.05 mmol), and
2-bromophenylboronic acid (264 mg, 1.8 mmol) were dissolved in
dioxane/H2O (3:1) (2 mL). The stirred mixture was heated to reflux
(preheated oil bath) and refluxed for 2 h until the reaction was finished
(TLC), before it was allowed to cool to ca. 20 °C. It was diluted (DCM,
20 mL), dried (Na2SO4), filtered, and adsorbed onto silica gel. Dry flash
chromatography (hexane/t-BuOMe, 4:1) gave the title compound 4a (378 mg,
98%) as colorless cubes, Ethyl
4-(3-Chloropyrid-4-yl)-6-methoxy-1,5-naphthyridine-3-carboxylate (4l).
(213 mg, 62%) as colorless needles. mp 95-97 °C (pentane), Rf 0.77
(t-BuOMe); (found: C, 59.5; H, 4.3; N, 12.2. C17H14ClN3O3 requires C,
59.4; H, 4.1; N, 12.2); λmax (DCM)/nm 229 (log ε 3.31), 249 (2.82), 261
inf (2.85), 267 (2.87), 318 (2.97), 327 (2.97); νmax/cm-1 2982w, 2922w,
1726 m (C=O), 1612w, 1587w, 1566w, 1499 m, 1464w, 1433w, 1402 m, 1371w,
1339 m, 1288 m, 1263 m, 1225 m, 1207w, 1180w, 1138w, 1121 m, 1096s, 1024
m, 980w, 932s, 901s, 854 m, 818w, 770w; δH (500 MHz; CD2Cl2) 9.35 (1H, s,
Ar H), 8.70 (1H, s, Ar H), 8.56 (1H, s, Ar H), 8.28 (1H, d, J = 9.0, Ar
H), 7.217.19 (2H, m, Ar H), 4.19 (3H, q, J = 6.6, OCH2), 3.69 (3H, s,
OCH3), 1.09 (3H, t, J = 7.0, CH3); δC (125 MHz; CD2Cl2); 165.3 (s), 163.0
(s), 149.2 (d), 148.6 (d), 147.3 (d), 144.8 (s), 144.5 (s), 143.0 (s),
140.4 (d), 139.3 (s), 131.3 (s), 125.5 (s), 125.3 (d), 118.9 (d), 62.1
(OCH2), 54.1 (OCH3), 13.8 (CH3); m/z (EI) 309 (MH+ -Cl, 19%), 308 (M+
-Cl, 100), 298 (3), 280 (65), 252 (7), 237 (4), 227 (4), 206 (4), 192
(5), 165 (5), 138 (2), 114 (2).
