$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure 2 for Synthesis of
N4-[3-(Dimethylamino)propyl]-N2-methyl-6-phenylthieno[3,2-d]-pyrimidine-2,4-diamine
4. To a solution of 3 (0.2 g, 0.58 mmol) in 1,4-dioxane (2 mL) was added
phenylboronic acid (0.1 g, 0.70 mmol). The mixture was thoroughly
degassed with nitrogen for 15 min, after which time Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 (20 mg,
0.03 mmol) was added, followed by (1 M) aqueous K2CO3 (0.61 mL, 0.61
mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred at 90 °C overnight and extracted
with ethyl acetate (4 × 15 mL). The combined organic layers were washed
with brine (3 × 10 mL), dried over Na2SO4, and concentrated in vacuo. The
remaining residue was subjected to column chromatography on silica gel,
with dichloromethane/methanol in a 8.5:1.5 (v/v) ratio as eluent, to
furnish 4.
N4-(3-(dimethylamino)propyl)-N2-methyl-6-(pyrimidin-5-yl)thieno[3,2-d]pyrimidine-2,4-diamine
36. According to GP2: Yield 59 mg, 59%. 1H NMR (300.1 MHz, [D6]DMSO): δ =
9.30 (s, 1H), 9.19 (s, 2H), 7.74 (s, 1H), 7.54 (br s, 1H), 6.38 (br s,
1h), 3.47 (dd, J = 12.6 Hz & 6.9 Hz, 2H), 2.81 (s, 3H), 2.30 (t, J = 6.9
Hz, 2H), 2.28 (s, 6H), 1.79 (t, J = 6.9 Hz, 2H); Anal. RP-HPLC tR = 5.50
min (method 2A, purity 95.0%); LRMS (APCI): m/z = LRMS (APCI): m/z =
343.1 [M+] (anal. calcd for C16H21N7S+: m/z = 343.16).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling, DMF solvent may also be used
