$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of polymer 12a: In a three-necked
100 mL flask, 4,7-bis(5-bromothien-2-yl)-2,1,3-benzothiadiazole (152.7
mg, 0.333 mmol), and 11 (227.5 mg, 0.333 mmol) were dissolved in toluene
(50 mL). 10% aqueous potassium carbonate solution (10 mL) and
tetrabutylammonium bromide (10.7 mg, 0.033 mmol, 10 mol%) were added to
the reaction solution. After purging with argon for 30 min, a suspension
of Pd(PPh3)4 (15.4 mg, 0.013 mmol, 4 mol%) in toluene was added. The
resulting mixture was purged for additional 15 min and refluxed for 72 h.
Phenylboronic acid (200 mg, 1.64 mmol) was added and the reaction mixture
was refluxed for additional 10 h. Iodobenzene (2.0 mL, 17.9 mmol) was
then added while continuously heating for 6 h. After cooling to r.t.,
CH2Cl2 (50 mL) was added. The organic phase was collected, washed with
water twice, and then dried over MgSO4•2H2O. After evaporation to a few
milliliters, the polymer was precipitated by the addition of methanol
(100 mL) and filtered through a Soxhlet thimble, which was then subjected
to Soxhlet extraction with methanol, heptane and chloroform. The polymer
12a was recovered as dark red-brown, slightly sticky flakes from the
chloroform fraction by rotary evaporation. Synthesis of polymer 12b: The
polymer 12b was obtained by the similar procedure as for the synthesis of
12a, starting from 11 (245.7 mg, 0.360 mmol), 6,6'-dibromoisoindigo,
(232.0 mg mg, 0.360 mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (16.6 mg, 0.014 mmol, 4 mol%) and
tetrabutylammonium bromide (11.6 mg, 0.036 mmol, 10 mol%). Extraction
with methanol, acetone, heptane and chloroform, 12b was obtained as a
deep-blue, plastic-like solid from the heptane fraction. Yield 185 mg (56
%). 1H NMR (CD2Cl2, 300 MHz) δ 9.01 (br, 2 H), 7.06 (br, 6 H), 4.41-3.57
(m, br, 8 H), 1.73-0.88 (m, br, 60 H). M W: 7600.
