$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
5,6-Didecyloxy-2,3,8,9-tetra(5-hexylthiophen-2-yl)naphtho[2,1-b:3,4-b']dithiophene
(11). To a 100 mL two-neck roundbottom flask was added 9 (304 mg, 0.35
mmol), 5-hexylthiophene-2-boronic acid2 (590 mg, 2.8 mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (50
mg), THF (50 mL) and 2 M K2CO3 (6.0 mL). The solution mixture was heated
to 80°C overnight under N2. After cooling to RT, the reaction mixture was
poured into water and extracted with dichloromethane (3 × 50 mL). The
combined organic phase was dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and evaporated to
dryness. The crude product was purified by silica gel column
chromatography using petroleum ether/dichloromethane as an eluent
affording the title product.
5,6-Didecyloxy-2,4,7,9-tetra(thiophen-2-yl)naphtho[2,1-b:3,4-b']dithiophene
(14). The synthetic procedure of 11 was followed using 10 (400 mg, 0.46
mmol), thiophene-2-boronic acid (470 mg, 3.7 mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (60 mg),
THF (80 mL), and 2 M K2CO3 (7.0 mL) affording the title product (225 mg,
55%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, δ): 7.67 (dd, J = 5.2 Hz, J = 1.2 Hz, 2H),
7.33 (dd, J = 5.2 Hz, J = 2.7 Hz, 2H), 7.21 (dd, J = 5.0 Hz, J = 1.0 Hz,
2H), 7.13-7.08 (m, 4H), 7.00 (dd, J = 5.2 Hz, J = 1.2 Hz, 2H), 6.33 (s,
2H), 3.99 (bs, 4H), 1.58-1.54 (m, 4H), 1.29-1.21 (m, 28H), 0.92 (t, J =
7.0 Hz, 6H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3, δ): 150.3, 139.4, 137.8, 133.7,
132.9, 132.6, 128.5, 127.8, 127.5, 126.9, 126.5, 126.3, 124.8, 124.1,
123.2, 74.1, 31.9, 30.3, 29.60, 29.57, 29.41, 29.37, 25.8, 22.7, 14.1.
HRMS (MALDI-TOF): calcd for C50H56O2S6: 880.2585; found: 876.2599.
