$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Compounds of Table 1. Procedure A.
(6S)-2-Nitro-6-{[2-(3-pyridinyl)benzyl]oxy}-6,7-dihydro-5H-imidazo[2,1-b][1,3]oxazine
(9) (Scheme 1A).
(6S)-6-[(2-Iodobenzyl)oxy]-2-nitro-6,7-dihydro-5H-imidazo[2,1-b][1,3]oxazine10
(127) (0.100 g, 0.249 mmol) and 3-pyridinylboronic acid (0.040 g, 0.325
mmol) were suspended in toluene/EtOH (5 mL/2 mL), and then aqueous K2CO3
(2 M, 1 mL) was added. The stirred mixture was purged with N2, treated
with Pd(dppf)Cl2 (9.5 mg, 0.013 mmol), and heated under reflux in an N2
atmosphere for 30 min. The resulting mixture was dilutedwithwater (10mL)
and extracted with EtOAc (3×15 mL). The dried (MgSO4) organic extracts
were adsorbed onto silica gel and chromatographed, eluting with EtOAc,
(6S)-6-[(5'-Fluoro[3,3'-bipyridin]-6-yl)methoxy]-2-nitro-6,7-dihydro-5H-imidazo[2,1-b][1,3]oxazine
(86). Reaction of bromide 156 and 5-fluoro-3-pyridinylboronic acid under
the Suzuki coupling conditions described in Procedure A for 21 h,
followed by chromatography of the product on silica gel, eluting with 5%
MeOH/EtOAc, gave 86 (55%) as a brown powder: mp 187 °C (dec); 1H NMR
[(CD3)2SO] δ 8.95 (br d, J = 1.9 Hz, 1 H), 8.86 (t, J = 1.8 Hz, 1 H),
8.63 (d, J = 2.7 Hz, 1 H), 8.22 (dd, J = 8.1, 2.4 Hz, 1 H), 8.17 (ddd, J
= 10.2, 2.6, 1.9 Hz, 1 H), 8.03 (s, 1 H), 7.50 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1 H), 4.83
(d, J = 13.3 Hz, 1 H), 4.79 (d, J = 13.3 Hz, 1 H), 4.73 (dt, J = 12.0,
2.6 Hz, 1 H), 4.51 (br d, J = 11.9 Hz, 1 H), 4.39-4.24 (m, 3 H). Anal.
(C17H14FN5O4∙0.25H2O) C, H. N: calcd, 18.63; found, 18.15. HPLC purity:
99.2%.
