$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of polymer 12a: In a three-necked 100 mL flask,
4,7-bis(5-bromothien-2-yl)-2,1,3-benzothiadiazole (152.7 mg, 0.333 mmol),
and 11 (227.5 mg, 0.333 mmol) were dissolved in toluene (50 mL). 10%
aqueous potassium carbonate solution (10 mL) and tetrabutylammonium
bromide (10.7 mg, 0.033 mmol, 10 mol%) were added to the reaction
solution. After purging with argon for 30 min, a suspension of Pd(PPh3)4
(15.4 mg, 0.013 mmol, 4 mol%) in toluene was added. The resulting mixture
was purged for additional 15 min and refluxed for 72 h. Phenylboronic
acid (200 mg, 1.64 mmol) was added and the reaction mixture was refluxed
for additional 10 h. Iodobenzene (2.0 mL, 17.9 mmol) was then added while
continuously heating for 6 h. After cooling to r.t., CH2Cl2 (50 mL) was
added. The organic phase was collected, washed with water twice, and then
dried over MgSO4•2H2O. After evaporation to a few milliliters, the
polymer was precipitated by the addition of methanol (100 mL) and
filtered through a Soxhlet thimble, which was then subjected to Soxhlet
extraction with methanol, heptane and chloroform. The polymer 12a was
recovered as dark red-brown, slightly sticky flakes from the chloroform
fraction by rotary evaporation. Yield 55 % (133 mg). 1H NMR (CD2Cl2, 300
MHz) δ 7.91-6.89 (m, br, 2 H), 4.39-4.27 (m, br, 4 H), 1.95-0.88 (m, br,
30 H). M W: 2900.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
