$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(4S*,4a′S*,10a′R*)-2-Amino-8′-(2-fluoropyridin-3-yl)-1,4a′-dimethyl-3′,4′,4a′,10a′-tetrahydro-2′H-spiro[imidazole-4,10′-pyrano[3,2-b]chromen]-5(1H)-one
(47). Charged a vial with 26 (19 mg, 0.038 mmol), dioxane (0.5 mL),
2-fluoropyridin-3-ylboronic acid (8.0 mg, 0.056 mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (4.4 mg,
0.0038 mmol), and 2N aq. Na2CO3 (56 μL, 0.11 mmol). Sparged reaction
mixture with N2 for 2 min, then heated to 90°C for 2h with stirring.
After cooling to rt, loaded reaction mixture directly on to a preparative
TLC plate (0.5 mm thickness, Rf = 0.51) eluting with 10% MeOH (containing
7N NH3)/DCM. Repurified impure product by a second preparative TLC plate
(0.5 mm thickness) eluting with 10% MeOH/DCM. Yield: 3 mg (20%). Purity:
87% by LC-MS (220 nm).
(4S*,4a′R*,10a′S*)-2-Amino-8′-(2-fluoropyridin-3-yl)-1,4a′-dimethyl-3′,4′,4a′,10a′-tetrahydro-2′H-spiro[imidazole-4,10′-pyrano[3,2-b]chromen]-5(1H)-one
(48). The title compound was prepared from 34 (5 mg, 0.01 mmol) according
to the procedure for compound 47. Crude was purified by preparative TLC
(0.5 mm thickness, Rf = 0.50), eluting with 10% MeOH (containing 7N NH3)/
DCM. Yield: 3 mg (53%). Purity: 97% by LC-MS (220 nm). Stereochemical
assignment was made by cocrystal structure of 48 with BACE1. 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.14 (d, J = 5 Hz, 1H), 7.75 (m, 1H), 7.41 (d, J = 9 Hz,
1H), 7.22 (m, 1H), 6.99 (br s, 1H), 6.94 (d, J = 9 Hz, 1H), 4.43 (br s,
2H), 4.08 (s, 1H), 4.04 (m, 1H), 3.56 (m, 1H), 3.19 (s, 3H), 2.09 (m,
1H), 1.92 (m, 2H), 1.73 (m, 1H), 1.45 (s, 3H). m/z (APCI-pos) M+1 = 397.
