$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Suzuki-Miyaura Cross-Coupling
Procedure for Preparation of Carbazole-Thiophene Oligomers. A mixture of
haloarene (1 equiv) and K2CO3 (1-2 equiv) in DME/water (10:1, ~0.2 mol
L-1) was bubbled with argon with stirring for 30 min. [Pd(PPh3)4] (ca.
2-3%, per reaction point) and boronic acid pinacol ester were added to
the mixture, and the resulting mixture was refluxed under an argon
atmosphere. The organic phase was separated, and theaqueous phase was
extracted with toluene, CH2Cl2, THF, or CHCl3. The combined organic phase
was washed with water, dried over anhydrous MgSO4, and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The residue was purified by column chromatography. An
analytically pure material was obtained by recycling GPC eluting with
CHCl3 and/or recrystallization. Compound 11 (0.10 g, 3.65 mmol) was
allowed to react with 13 (37 mg, 0.109 mmol) in the presence of K2CO3
(0.10 g, 0.729 mmol) and [Pd(PPh3)4] (25 mg, 21.9 μmol) for 15 h. The
crude material was purified by column chromatography (SiO2,
toluene/hexane = 1:3). Compound 15 (0.40 g, 1.13 mmol) was allowed to
react with 16 (0.18 mg, 0.871 mmol) in the presence of K2CO3 (0.24 mg,
1.74 mmol) and [Pd(PPh3)4] (30 mg, 26.1 μmol) for 16 h. The crude
material was purified by column chromatography (SiO2, toluene/hexane =
1:5). Compound 18 as pale yellow solid, yield 0.16 g, 51%. Mp 136-137 °C;
1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.24 (1H, d, J = 1.8 Hz), 8.23 (1H, d, J = 1.9
Hz), 7.74 (1H, dd, J = 8.5 and 1.8 Hz), 7.55 (1H, dd, J = 8.6 and 1.9
Hz), 7.36 (1H, d, J = 8.5 Hz), 7.34 (1H, dd, J = 3.5 and 1.1 Hz), 7.28
(1H, dd, J = 5.1 and 1.1 Hz), 7.26 (1H, d, J = 8.6 Hz), 7.12 (1H, dd, J =
5.1 and 3.5 Hz), 4.30 (2H, q, J = 7.2 Hz), 1.41 (3H, t, J = 7.2 Hz); 13C
NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ 145.5, 139.7, 139.0, 128.7, 128.1, 126.2, 125.0,
124.6, 123.9, 123.4, 122.4, 122.2, 118.1, 111.9, 110.1, 109.1, 37.8,
13.9; UV-vis (CH2Cl2): λmax abs 304 nm; MALDI-TOF-MS (Dith, positive):
m/z 356.57 [(M + H)+]. Elemental analysis calcd (%) for C18H14BrNS: C,
60.68; H, 3.96; N, 3.93%. Found: C, 60.51; H, 3.95; N, 3.94%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki-Miyaura cross coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
