$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Suzuki Coupling of
Intermediate 8 with Corresponding Boronic Acids. In a microwave vial,
intermediate 8 (0.33 mmol), arylboronic acid or boronate (83 mg, 0.67
mmol), and sodium bicarbonate (56.0 mg, 0.67 mmol) were mixed with DME (8
mL) and water (2 mL). The mixture was purged with N2 for 10 min.
Pd(PPh3)4 (57.7 mg, 0.05 mmol) was added to the mixture, and the mixture
was microwaved for 80 min at 115 °C. The reaction mixture was cooled to
rt and concentrated under vacuum. The residue was diluted with water (10
mL) and extracted with dichloromethane (thrice). The organic layers were
combined, dried over sodium sulfate, and concentrated under vacuum. The
residue was purified by flash chromatography on a silica gel column using
MeOH-DCM as the eluent. Pure fractions were combined and evaporated under
vacuum. The pure final compound as crystalline material in 40-80% yield.
(S)-1-Ethyl-3-(5-(1-methoxypropan-2-yloxy)-6-(pyridin-3-yl)-thiazolo[5,4-b]pyridin-2-yl)urea
(14). Yield: 50%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 1.10 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H),
1.28 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 3H), 3.19 (quin, J = 6.8 Hz, 2H), 3.26 (s, 3H),
3.46-3.56 (m, 2H), 5.35-5.53 (m, 1H), 6.70 (br s, 1H), 7.48 (dd, J = 7.5,
5.0 Hz, 1H), 7.97-8.21 (m, 2H), 8.56 (d, J = 4.5 Hz, 1H), 8.83 (s, 1H),
10.74 (br, 1H). HRMS: m/z (ES+) 388.1434 (MH+) for C18H21N5O3S.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, reactant assumed, Suzuki coupling, PdCl2(PPh3)2
catalyst may also be used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Thiazolopyridine Ureas as Novel Antitubercular Agents Acting through
Inhibition of DNA Gyrase B
